<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't sells 98 percent in coffee stock sale.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't sells 98 percent in coffee stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government sold 147,123 or 98.08 percent of the 150,000 60-kg bags of coffee stocks offered to all segments of the coffee sector in its auction today, said an official from the Banco do Brasil.</p>
<p>Total revenue for the government was 24.55 million reais ($22.94 million).  </p>
<p>The auction, which lasted over four hours, saw very good demand, with closing prices up to 20 reais per bag higher than initial levels set by the government.</p>
<p>Yesterday the Sao Paulo State Coffee Industry Union said that Brazilian coffee roasters are now experiencing problems obtaining green coffee for roasting in the domestic market.</p>
